WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.940
Why would a well-fed mouse suddenly start eating?

2
00:00:06.983 --> 00:00:11.863
Researchers put a light-sensitive switch into a small group of neurons at the base

3
00:00:11.863 --> 00:00:12.863
of its brain.

4
00:00:13.517 --> 00:00:17.697
When they shone light on those neurons, the well-fed mouse began eating within

5
00:00:17.697 --> 00:00:18.697
minutes.

6
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.647
That raises two questions.

7
00:00:21.627 --> 00:00:22.627
Why is food worth seeking?

8
00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:25.487
And how does the brain learn where to find it?

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.000
Hunger answers the first.

10
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.260
Hunger changes how much food is worth right now, and circuits in the hypothalamus

11
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.560
are thought to help set that.

12
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.980
Dopamine neurons in the midbrain help with the second, and what they report is

13
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:40.980
surprising.

14
00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:43.493
They do not simply report the reward.

15
00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:47.373
They report how much better or worse things went than predicted.

16
00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.587
Picture two bars over a cup of juice.

17
00:00:51.447 --> 00:00:52.847
One shows what was predicted.

18
00:00:53.807 --> 00:00:55.067
The other shows what arrived.

19
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.860
The gap between them is the error.

20
00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:02.123
When the juice is better than predicted, the gap is positive.

21
00:01:03.003 --> 00:01:04.543
The neuron fires a brief burst.

22
00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:07.993
Now the juice arrives exactly as predicted.

23
00:01:08.993 --> 00:01:09.993
What does the neuron do?

24
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:20.743
Nothing. With no gap, there is no error, and the firing stays steady.

25
00:01:21.783 --> 00:01:25.783
When the reward is worse than predicted, or missing, the gap is negative.

26
00:01:26.723 --> 00:01:27.843
Firing pauses briefly.

27
00:01:28.933 --> 00:01:33.513
If the same juice comes every trial, the prediction moves part of the way toward it

28
00:01:33.513 --> 00:01:34.513
each time.

29
00:01:34.983 --> 00:01:37.423
So the error at the juice shrinks toward zero.

30
00:01:38.323 --> 00:01:40.783
An uncertain reward always leaves some surprise.

31
00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:45.347
With learning, the burst moves to the tone that announces the juice.

32
00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.427
Good news from a cue counts as an error too.

33
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:53.550
Hunger and satiety change how much the reward is worth in the first place.

34
00:01:54.583 --> 00:02:00.103
Keep the scope. This holds for many, not all, dopamine neurons, in trained monkeys

35
00:02:00.103 --> 00:02:01.103
and rodents.

36
00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:03.113
It describes a signal.

37
00:02:03.933 --> 00:02:06.773
A recording alone does not show that the signal teaches.

38
00:02:07.773 --> 00:02:09.333
And it says nothing about pleasure.

39
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:16.017
Carry one idea. Dopamine bursts and pauses report better or worse than predicted,

40
00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:18.497
and hunger shapes what the reward is worth.
